#: ../../../support.md:1
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:3
msgid ""
"Different types of questions or discussions correspond to different avenues "
"of communication. Please check the descriptions below to ensure you choose "
"the right method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:7
msgid ""
"If you need help troubleshooting your system, first search existing "
"discussions to see if others have encountered a similar issue and whether a "
"solution already exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:11
msgid ""
"If not, feel free to ask a new question using one of the support options "
"below. Please avoid contacting developers or maintainers directly, as public "
"support channels allow the whole community to participate and benefit from "
"shared solutions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:16
msgid "Getting help"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:18
msgid "Robotics Stack Exchange"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:20
msgid ""
"For general usage questions and troubleshooting help, please ask on "
"[Robotics Stack Exchange](https://robotics.stackexchange.com/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:23
msgid ""
"Make sure to tag your question with **gazebo** (and any other relevant tags) "
"so it can be easily found by the community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:26
msgid ""
"When asking a question, please include enough information for others to "
"understand the problem, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:28
msgid "Your operating system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:29
msgid "Gazebo version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:30
msgid "What you were trying to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:31
msgid "What happened instead, including any warnings or error messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:33
msgid ""
"Providing clear and complete details makes it much easier for others to help "
"you find a solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:36
msgid "Gazebo Discourse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:38
msgid ""
"To start a discussion with other Gazebo community members, visit the Gazebo "
"category on Open Robotics Discourse: [Gazebo Discourse](https://discourse."
"openrobotics.org/c/gazebo/95)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:42
msgid ""
"Discourse is intended for higher-level discussions, such as best practices, "
"design considerations, or general questions about using Gazebo, rather than "
"debugging specific errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:46
msgid "Zulip chat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:48
msgid ""
"For real-time communication with Gazebo developers and users, you can join "
"the Open Robotics Zulip workspace: [Open Robotics Zulip server](https://"
"openrobotics.zulipchat.com/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:52
msgid ""
"Zulip is well suited for quick questions, development discussion, and "
"collaboration. Please note that responses may vary depending on time zones "
"and availability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:56
msgid "Pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:58
msgid ""
"If you would like to contribute a fix or improvement directly, you are "
"welcome to open a pull request against the appropriate Gazebo repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:61
msgid "Please make sure to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:62
msgid "Follow the pull request template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:63
msgid "Target the correct branch for your change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:65
msgid ""
"Guidance on branch selection, contribution workflow, and general "
"contribution etiquette is described in the contributing guide: [Contributing "
"to Gazebo](https://gazebosim.org/docs/all/contributing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:69
msgid "Reporting bugs and requesting features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:71
msgid ""
"If you identify a bug, have a suggestion for improvement, or would like to "
"request a new feature, please open an issue in the appropriate repository on "
"GitHub: [Gazebo Sim](https://github.com/gazebosim)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:76
msgid "Before opening a new issue, please:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:77
msgid "Search existing issues to see if the problem has already been reported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:78
msgid "Use the provided issue template and fill out all relevant sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../support.md:80
msgid ""
"Using the issue templates and providing complete information helps "
"maintainers and contributors understand and address issues more efficiently."
msgstr ""
